{"name":"Railroad Ties","hex":"#544540","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"railroad ties","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of railroad tie"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/railroad_ties"}],"entries":[{"title":"Railroad tie","blocks":[{"text":"A railroad tie, crosstie, railway tie or railway sleeper is a rectangular support for the rails in railroad tracks. Generally laid perpendicular to the rails, ties transfer loads to the track ballast and subgrade, hold the rails upright and keep them spaced to the correct gauge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Railroad_tieswoodconcrete.jpg/330px-Railroad_tieswoodconcrete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Railroad_tie"},{"title":"Rail transport","blocks":[{"text":"Rail transport is a mode of transport using wheeled vehicles running on tracks, which usually consist of two parallel steel rails. Rail transport is one of the two primary means of land transport, next to road transport. It is used for about 8% of passenger and freight transport globally, thanks to its energy efficiency and potentially high speed. Additionally, the track spreads the weight of the train which means larger amounts can be carried than with trucks on roads."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Alaska_Railroad_oil_train_at_Nenna.jpg/330px-Alaska_Railroad_oil_train_at_Nenna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rail_transport"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Kilmarnock_%26_Troon_railway_sleeper.JPG/500px-Kilmarnock_%26_Troon_railway_sleeper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Kilmarnock_%26_Troon_railway_sleeper.JPG/1280px-Kilmarnock_%26_Troon_railway_sleeper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Kilmarnock_%26_Troon_railway_sleeper.JPG/500px-Kilmarnock_%26_Troon_railway_sleeper.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Stone block from the Kilmarnock and Troon Railway","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKilmarnock_%26_Troon_railway_sleeper.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Wood_tie.webp/500px-Wood_tie.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Wood_tie.webp/1280px-Wood_tie.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Wood_tie.webp/500px-Wood_tie.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Wood tie on the BNSF Railway in La Crosse, Wisconsin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWood_tie.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Concrete_sleeper_tie.webp/500px-Concrete_sleeper_tie.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Concrete_sleeper_tie.webp/1280px-Concrete_sleeper_tie.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Concrete_sleeper_tie.webp/500px-Concrete_sleeper_tie.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Concrete tie on the BNSF Railway in La Crosse, Wisconsin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AConcrete_sleeper_tie.webp"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Pine_Creek_Rail_Steel_Sleepers_DSC03637.jpg/500px-Pine_Creek_Rail_Steel_Sleepers_DSC03637.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe